            "reviewBody": "Wow, what an easy and delicious dish to prepare! I worried there might not be enough seasonings but this dish was flavourful and refreshing."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Faye"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Toasted the quinoa for 5 minutes. Added chopped spinach and olive oil and a bit more cumin. Got rave reviews at holiday party potluck.",
            "datePublished": "2016-12-27T15:22:21.907Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "quiltersammy"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is good but I thought it needed some garlic powder, a splash of Louisiana hot sauce and a seeded, devained and diced fresh jalapeno. I used my microwave rice cooker and followed the instructions on the side of the quinoa box.",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-22T09:12:24.377Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Allrecipes Member"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Fantastic! Made it as is, and it was very good - 4.5 stars as written. But I made a couple of slight tweaks to really add that little extra:\n\n- Extra 1T lime juice\n- Extra 1/8t of cumin\n- Add 1/8t garlic powder\n\nTo me, that added the extra \"dressing\" and tiny extra punch that made this out of this world! On a side portion, I also mixed in a bit of oil/balsamic as other suggested, but I thought that confused the taste of the lime/cumin. It was still good, but a bit off.\n\nWill add this to my staples, SOOOO easy to make especially with cooked quinoa at the ready!",
            "datePublished": "2013-01-16T18:48:31.033Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "GREENIE2600"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is an easy, delicious, and very refreshing salad. I added half of a minced jalapeño to the dressing, which worked well. The recipe says it makes two servings, but it's more like one serving if you're eating it as an entree. You can probably reduce the amount of avocado, too. This would be a spectacular lunch or dinner for those summer days when it's too hot to think.",
            "datePublished": "2015-02-08T15:08:59.220Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "cmmunchkin"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was a good base. As others said, there isn't really enough dressing, and I felt like it needed a little more kick. I mixed up an olive oil and balsamic dressing with a bit more cumin to pour over the spinach leaves and a bit more on the salad. I like the idea of using these flavors on the quinoa.",
            "datePublished": "2011-09-16T07:34:01.383Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "SLJ6"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent .....and I love quinoa so this is just another delicious way to enjoy it....my only mini change was to cook my quinoa in chicken broth instead of water. Loved this healthy and light dinner. Thanks Gitano!",
            "datePublished": "2011-04-28T15:10:16.310Z"
          },
